      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m having a hard time figuring out what the use of uninitialized variable was that https://ci.chromium.org/ui/p/chromium/builders/try/linux_chromium_msan_rel_ng/10596/test-results is referring to, though it indicated that it was on this line in the previous patch.\n\nMy best guess is that I was passing attachmentInfo.depthSlice in here directly, but in the code we\u0027re replacing that variable would have only been accessed when the texture dimension was 3D. I feel like the depth slice should always be initialized to at least MAX_INT (because that the uninitialized enum value) but at least but only using the value here if the dimension is 3D it stays closer to the original code.",
