      "message": "MSan tells you where the value comes from, but that was truncated in the link you pasted. Looking at the full logs it says:\n\n```\n  Uninitialized value was created by an allocation of \u0027beginCmd\u0027 in the stack frame\n    #0 0x555559de3359 in dawn::native::vulkan::Texture::ClearTexture(dawn::native::vulkan::CommandRecordingContext*, dawn::native::SubresourceRange const\u0026, dawn::native::TextureBase::ClearValue) ./../../third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/TextureVk.cpp:1099:17\n```\n\nWe need to look at the C++ rules for initialization but it seems that something doesn\u0027t get default initialized there.\n\nAlso I don\u0027t see any changes done in this reland?",
